{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-hebrews-013",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 13,
  "title": "Hebrews 13",
  "display_title": "Hebrews 13",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "hebrews",
  "book": "Hebrews",
  "bookName": "Hebrews",
  "bookOrder": 58,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 13,
  "sortOrder": 58013,
  "verseCount": 25,
  "aliases": [
    "Heb",
    "He"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Let brotherly love continue.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Be not forgetful to entertain strangers: for thereby some have entertained angels unawares.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Remember them that are in bonds, as bound with them; and them which suffer adversity, as being yourselves also in the body.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Marriage is honourable in all, and the bed undefiled: but whoremongers and adulterers God will judge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Let your conversation be without covetousness; and be content with such things as ye have: for he hath said, I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "So that we may boldly say, The Lord is my helper, and I will not fear what man shall do unto me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Remember them which have the rule over you, who have spoken unto you the word of God: whose faith follow, considering the end of their conversation.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Jesus Christ the same yesterday, and to day, and for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Be not carried about with divers and strange doctrines. For it is a good thing that the heart be established with grace; not with meats, which have not profited them that have been occupied therein.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "We have an altar, whereof they have no right to eat which serve the tabernacle.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "For the bodies of those beasts, whose blood is brought into the sanctuary by the high priest for sin, are burned without the camp.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Wherefore Jesus also, that he might sanctify the people with his own blood, suffered without the gate.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Let us go forth therefore unto him without the camp, bearing his reproach.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "For here have we no continuing city, but we seek one to come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "By him therefore let us offer the sacrifice of praise to God continually, that is, the fruit of our lips giving thanks to his name.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "But to do good and to communicate forget not: for with such sacrifices God is well pleased.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Obey them that have the rule over you, and submit yourselves: for they watch for your souls, as they that must give account, that they may do it with joy, and not with grief: for that is unprofitable for you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Pray for us: for we trust we have a good conscience, in all things willing to live honestly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "But I beseech you the rather to do this, that I may be restored to you the sooner.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Now the God of peace, that brought again from the dead our Lord Jesus, that great shepherd of the sheep, through the blood of the everlasting covenant,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Make you perfect in every good work to do his will, working in you that which is wellpleasing in his sight, through Jesus Christ; to whom be glory for ever and ever. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "And I beseech you, brethren, suffer the word of exhortation: for I have written a letter unto you in few words.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Know ye that our brother Timothy is set at liberty; with whom, if he come shortly, I will see you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Salute all them that have the rule over you, and all the saints. They of Italy salute you.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:hebrews:13:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Grace be with you all. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Hebrews 13:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:hebrews:13:25"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
